{"v":15,"id":"e08","kid":"emma","title":"Yuan Longping: The Father of Hybrid Rice","zh":"袁隆平：杂交水稻之父","level":"B1","genre":"人物传记","src":"facts","sum":"袁隆平看到饥荒中的人们，立志让水稻增产。他和团队多年寻找，终于培育出杂交水稻，帮助全世界数以亿计的人吃饱饭。","words":303,"paras":[{"t":"In the early 1960s, many families in China did not have enough food. A young teacher named Yuan Longping saw hungry people on the streets, and he made a decision: he would find a way to grow more rice.","w":[[0,2,"in",-1],[3,6,"the",-1],[7,12,"early",-1],[20,24,"many",-1],[25,33,"families",-1],[34,36,"in",-1],[37,42,"china",-1],[43,46,"did",-1],[47,50,"not",-1],[51,55,"have",-1],[56,62,"enough",-1],[63,67,"food",-1],[69,70,"a",-1],[71,76,"young",-1],[77,84,"teacher",-1],[85,90,"named",-1],[91,95,"Yuan",-1],[96,104,"Longping",-1],[105,108,"saw",-1],[109,115,"hungry",-1],[116,122,"people",-1],[123,125,"on",-1],[126,129,"the",-1],[130,137,"streets",-1],[139,142,"and",-1],[143,145,"he",-1],[146,150,"made",1],[151,152,"a",1],[153,161,"decision",1],[163,165,"he",-1],[166,171,"would",-1],[172,176,"find",-1],[177,178,"a",-1],[179,182,"way",-1],[183,185,"to",-1],[186,190,"grow",-1],[191,195,"more",-1],[196,200,"rice",-1]]},{"t":"Yuan was born in Beijing in 1930. He studied agriculture at university and then taught at a farming school in Hunan Province. In 1961, while he was walking in a rice field, he noticed one rice plant that was taller and stronger than the others. It had many more grains. This gave him an idea. If he could combine the good qualities of different rice plants, he might create a new kind of rice with a much higher yield.","w":[[0,4,"Yuan",-1],[5,8,"was",-1],[9,13,"born",-1],[14,16,"in",-1],[17,24,"Beijing",-1],[25,27,"in",-1],[34,36,"he",-1],[37,44,"studied",-1],[45,56,"agriculture",-1],[57,59,"at",-1],[60,70,"university",-1],[71,74,"and",-1],[75,79,"then",-1],[80,86,"taught",-1],[87,89,"at",-1],[90,91,"a",-1],[92,99,"farming",-1],[100,106,"school",-1],[107,109,"in",-1],[110,115,"Hunan",2],[116,124,"province",2],[126,128,"in",-1],[135,140,"while",-1],[141,143,"he",-1],[144,147,"was",-1],[148,155,"walking",-1],[156,158,"in",-1],[159,160,"a",-1],[161,165,"rice",14],[166,171,"field",14],[173,175,"he",-1],[176,183,"noticed",-1],[184,187,"one",-1],[188,192,"rice",-1],[193,198,"plant",-1],[199,203,"that",-1],[204,207,"was",-1],[208,214,"taller",-1],[215,218,"and",-1],[219,227,"stronger",-1],[228,232,"than",-1],[233,236,"the",-1],[237,243,"others",-1],[245,247,"it",-1],[248,251,"had",-1],[252,256,"many",-1],[257,261,"more",-1],[262,268,"grains",-1],[270,274,"this",-1],[275,279,"gave",3],[280,283,"him",3],[284,286,"an",3],[287,291,"idea",3],[293,295,"if",-1],[296,298,"he",-1],[299,304,"could",-1],[305,312,"combine",-1],[313,316,"the",-1],[317,321,"good",-1],[322,331,"qualities",-1],[332,334,"of",-1],[335,344,"different",-1],[345,349,"rice",-1],[350,356,"plants",-1],[358,360,"he",-1],[361,366,"might",-1],[367,373,"create",-1],[374,375,"a",-1],[376,379,"new",-1],[380,384,"kind",-1],[385,387,"of",-1],[388,392,"rice",-1],[393,397,"with",-1],[398,399,"a",-1],[400,404,"much",-1],[405,411,"higher",-1],[412,417,"yield",-1]]},{"t":"This kind of rice is called hybrid rice. At that time, many experts believed it was impossible to grow hybrid rice successfully. Yuan and his team did not give up. For years they searched rice fields across China and looked at thousands of plants. Finally, in 1970, a member of his team found a special wild rice plant on Hainan Island. It was the key they needed. By 1973, they had produced successful hybrid rice, and a few years later it was being planted widely in China.","w":[[0,4,"this",-1],[5,9,"kind",-1],[10,12,"of",-1],[13,17,"rice",-1],[18,20,"is",-1],[21,27,"called",-1],[28,34,"hybrid",0],[35,39,"rice",0],[41,43,"at",-1],[44,48,"that",-1],[49,53,"time",-1],[55,59,"many",-1],[60,67,"experts",-1],[68,76,"believed",-1],[77,79,"it",-1],[80,83,"was",-1],[84,94,"impossible",-1],[95,97,"to",-1],[98,102,"grow",-1],[103,109,"hybrid",0],[110,114,"rice",0],[115,127,"successfully",-